# Paths that need no review when a PR changes nothing else (PROC-0001, "Review by risk"). review-gate reads this
# file from the default branch, and only a PR into the default branch can be exempt. A PR into any other branch
# always needs a review. One path per line; a path ending in / covers a folder; a line starting with ! takes a
# path back out, and the last line that matches a file decides. Anything not listed here needs a review.
#
# Keep it to prose that no build, test, gate or package reads. The required checks still run on an exempt PR, so a
# broken link or a gate that reads a listed file still fails there; this list only drops the review.
# Not listed, on purpose: README.md (packed into every NuGet package), AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md
# (rules the reviewers and agents follow), LICENSE, NOTICE, SECURITY.md and TRADEMARKS.md (legal and security
# policy), docs/evidence/ (records gates rely on), docs/install/ (ships in the install artefact), the t433 and m6
# design notes at the top of docs/ (tests and gates read some of them), and packages/**/Contracts/*.md (contracts,
# not prose). The gate never exempts an agent instruction file (AGENTS.md, AGENTS.override.md, CLAUDE.md or
# CLAUDE.local.md) at any depth, even inside a folder listed here. This file is under .github/, so changing it is
# itself risky.
SUPPORT.md
docs/examples/
docs/operations/
